# WLISTTX.KEY - the rows of a list window dragged (TEST/WLISTT.C /DRAG),
# over the seed's three items: TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WLISTTX.SNP, checked by
# TEST/dragchk.py.  A press moved 4 pixels is a click, 5 a drag; the
# list is its own target, the row under the pointer framed.  SHIFT-Q
# (WM_CANCELMODE to the list window) while only pressed leaves the
# press the list box's own, a click; during a drag it ends it, as do
# ESC and the capture lost (CTRL-Q).  A double click opens its row and
# starts no drag.  The list destroyed during a drag (CTRL-SHIFT-Q) gives
# no note.
S START
M 1.1 DOWN ROW 0
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 0 4 0
S ARMED
M 1.1 UP ROW 0 4 0
S CLICK
M 1.1 DOWN ROW 1
K SHIFT-Q
S ARMCANC
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 1 8 0
S ARMMOVE
M 1.1 UP ROW 1 8 0
S ARMUP
M 1.1 DOWN ROW 0
M 1.1 UP ROW 0
M 1.1 DBL ROW 0
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 0 8 0
S DBLMOVE
M 1.1 UP ROW 0 8 0
S DBLUP
M 1.1 DOWN ROW 0
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 0 0 5
S STARTED
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 1
S OVER1
M 1.1 MOVE AT 5 -5
S OUTSIDE
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 1
M 1.1 UP ROW 1
S DROPPED
M 1.1 DOWN ROW 0
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 0 -5 0
K ESC
S ESC
M 1.1 UP ROW 0 -5 0
S ESCUP
M 1.1 DOWN ROW 0
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 0 8 0
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 1
K SHIFT-Q
S CANCEL
M 1.1 UP ROW 1
S CANCELUP
M 1.1 DOWN ROW 0
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 0 8 0
K CTRL-Q
S LOST
M 1.1 UP ROW 0 8 0
S LOSTUP
M 1.1 DOWN ROW 1
M 1.1 MOVE ROW 1 8 0
K CTRL-SHIFT-Q
S GONE
K ESC
